course: dictionary
lesson: 13252
title: Gilded and golden words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Gilded is a tricky word, but the clues around it help. «The old picture frame was gilded, so it shone like gold in the sunlight.» The words shone like gold are the clue. Gilded means covered with a thin layer of gold.
explain: Sometimes gilded describes how something looks, not what it is made of. «Her gilded life looked perfect from the outside, but she felt lonely inside.» The word but tells you the shine was only on the outside. So gilded can mean rich and fancy, but only on the surface.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «covered with a thin layer of gold» still make sense in the frame sentence? Yes, so you have it right.
fact: Gilded comes from the verb gild: gild, gilds, gilded, gilding.
fact: «Gilded» means covered with a thin layer of gold or gold-coloured paint.
fact: «Gilded» can also mean looking rich and fancy, sometimes only on the outside.
fact: A «gilded cage» is a comfortable, rich life where you are not free.
fact: The «Gilded Age» was a time in US history, about 1870 to 1900, when some people became very rich while many others were poor.
exercise: «The gilded frame shone in the candlelight.» What does gilded mean? | *Covered with a thin layer of gold | Made of wood and painted green | Broken and dusty | Very cold to touch
exercise: «She felt trapped in her gilded cage, with plenty of money but no freedom.» What does a gilded cage mean? | A real cage made from gold bars | A small room with no windows | *A comfortable, rich life where you are not free
exercise: Which phrase names a time in US history when some people were very rich and many were poor? | The Bronze Age | The Stone Age | The Ice Age | *The Gilded Age
test: Which word is the past form of gild? | *gilded | gilding | gild | gilds
test: «The palace ceiling was gilded, so it looked like real gold.» What does gilded mean here? | *Covered with a thin layer of gold | Cracked and old | Painted blue | Very dusty
exam: Which meaning fits «a gilded life» that looks perfect but is not? | *Looking rich and fancy, but only on the outside | Very quick and busy | Covered in mud | Full of music
